  "question": {
    "text": "In an adiabatic process, the density of a diatomic gas becomes <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>32</mn></math><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi></math>&nbsp;times its initial value. The final pressure of the gas is found to be&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi></math> times the initial pressure. The value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi></math> is:",
